flowchart LR
    subgraph aws[AWS VPC]
        workload[AWS workload]
        vpcresolver[Route 53 VPC Resolver]
        outbound[Outbound Resolver endpoint]
        inbound[Inbound Resolver endpoint]
        phz[AWS private hosted zone or VPC DNS namespace]
    end

    subgraph onprem[On-premises network]
        client[On-premises client]
        dns[On-premises DNS resolver]
        auth[On-premises authoritative DNS]
    end

    transport[Existing private transport: Site-to-Site VPN or Direct Connect]

    workload -->|query on-premises private suffix| vpcresolver
    vpcresolver -->|Resolver forwarding rule| outbound
    outbound --> transport --> dns
    dns -->|query and answer| auth

    client -->|query AWS private suffix| dns
    dns -->|conditional forwarder| transport
    transport --> inbound --> vpcresolver --> phz

    note[Conceptual study diagram only\nOutbound: AWS asks on-premises\nInbound: on-premises asks AWS\nTransport carries DNS packets but does not configure DNS forwarding]
    vpcresolver --- note
